{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nRe-running `rebar review-code` (attested snapshot) on bug-introducing changes shows the escaped\ndefect landing at priority 0.60 / validity 1.0 on criteria that cannot block.\n\n- `c3aec3eae6` (Gerrit 1560; bug `earthen-flayed-baboon` = `1d71-a76c-04f6-4642`, closed) produced a\n  `correctness`/`edge-cases` finding that IS the bug — advisory only because **neither id is among\n  the 21 keys of `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json`**.\n- `d2dea317ec` (Gerrit 1727) produced a `concurrency` finding at 0.60 naming a real defect (a\n  stand-aside still stamps the sweep clock), advisory because `concurrency` is `\"blocking_enabled\":\n  false` at `\"block_threshold\": 0.95` (`criteria_routing.json:151-158`).\n\n`tests` and `regression` block at 0.54 (`criteria_routing.json:110-118`, `:159-166`). The code-v4\nreplay (`61d50b0513`, `docs/experiments/replay_code_v4_would_block.py`) has not been run for these\nthree. Approved 2026-08-21.\n\n**Facts corrected against the tree.**\n1. **`correctness` and `edge-cases` are BASE-REVIEWER dimensions, not overlays.** They come from the\n   base reviewer's evidence contract (`llm/reviewers/code-review-base.md:33-34`) and are NOT in the\n   closed `OVERLAY_IDS` enum (`llm/code_review/registry.py:38-54`). `regression` has the same shape;\n   its `_comment` states it — for such a dimension \"`exec`/`applies_to` are inert here and only the\n   posture/threshold/blocking_enabled fields are consulted\" (`criteria_routing.json:159-160`). An\n   `exec: AGENT` approach is therefore inert.\n2. **Real schema keys are `default_posture`/`block_threshold`**, not `posture`/`threshold`.\n3. **Unknown-criterion default lives in the shared resolver.** `registry.threshold_for`\n   (`registry.py:490-514`) delegates to `rebar.llm.criteria.model.threshold_for`\n   (`llm/criteria/model.py:45-88`); constant `registry.py:148` (`DEFAULT_BLOCK_THRESHOLD=0.95`).\n4. **`tests/unit/llm/code_review/` does not exist** — no `tests/unit/llm/` directory at all;\n   `pytest tests/unit/llm/code_review -k routing` errors \"file or directory not found\". Code-review\n   tests live at `tests/unit/test_code_review_*.py`.\n5. **`scripts/check_criteria_routing_parity` does not exist.** The only criteria-routing parity gate\n   (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:548-560`) covers plan-review's routing file.\n6. **`scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py` is the wrong script** — it confines the deprecated\n   phrase \"success criteria\"/\"SC\" (`:2,21-22`), not criterion ids. Out of scope.\n7. **No committed tool computes an \"amended-after\" rate**; that metric is dropped here.\n8. **`replay_code_v4_would_block.py:45-55` hard-codes `_BLOCKING_SET`** as a literal 8-tuple for its\n   printed summary (`:106`), while the gate it applies comes from `threshold_for` (`:64`) — any\n   posture flip silently desynchronises the two.\n\n## Approach\n1. Add `correctness` and `edge-cases` to `criteria_routing.json` as BASE-REVIEWER rows shaped like\n   `regression`: `\"exec\": \"AGENT\"`, `\"applies_to\": []`, `\"default_posture\": \"advisory\"`,\n   `\"block_threshold\": 0.95`, `\"blocking_enabled\": false`, plus a `_comment` naming this ticket and\n   `c3aec3eae6`. Findings are then scored explicitly rather than via the unknown-criterion default\n   (`criteria/model.py:70-73`).\n2. Measure friction at 0.54 for `correctness`, `edge-cases` and `concurrency` with\n   `docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py --tracker <checkout> --emit <path>`, which\n   pools findings by their `criteria` list generically (`:86`) — no code change needed for new ids.\n   Record the columns the existing table defines\n   (`docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md:80`): surviving, would-block, % of\n   surviving, changes hit, % of all changes, mean validity, val<0.5 — plus whether the escaped-bug\n   set (`c3aec3eae6`, `d2dea317ec`) is recalled. Commit as\n   `## Code-v4 friction replay at 0.54 (correctness, edge-cases, concurrency)`.\n3. Flip to `\"blocking_enabled\": true` / `\"block_threshold\": 0.54` only where the measured **% of all\n   changes** is at or under **8.0%** — the operator-accepted budget recorded in the `tests` entry's\n   `_comment` (\"blocks 99 changes / 8.0%, operator-accepted\", `criteria_routing.json:110`), not a\n   figure in the calibration document. Others stay advisory with their number recorded. No\n   currently-blocking criterion's threshold changes.\n4. Derive `_BLOCKING_SET` in `replay_code_v4_would_block.py` from `registry.routing_index()`\n   filtered on `blocking_enabled`, replacing the literal tuple, so the summary cannot drift from the\n   posture actually applied.\n\n## Constraints\n- **Corpus is not in git** — it lives in a checkout's `.tickets-tracker`\n  (`replay_code_v4_would_block.py:16-18`). Step 2 runs once by the author; its OUTPUT lands. Every\n  CI-checked criterion below is corpus-free and CI-provider-free (`project.portability`);\n  `replay_code_v4_would_block.py` with no `--tracker` runs a self-check that exits 0 today.\n- **Adding keys widens the canonical vocabulary.** The gate registers `canonical=lambda:\n  frozenset(routing_index())` (`registry.py:167-171`), so `registry.effective_criteria(repo_root)`\n  grows. Readers: `llm/evals/eval.py:414`, `llm/evals/eval_solver.py:206`,\n  `llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:449`, `llm/workflow/criterion_preview.py:551`. Intended; asserted.\n- **`.rebar/criteria_routing.json` re-tunes `code_review.concurrency`** (adds `trigger_tokens`,\n  `applies_to`). `criteria.overlay.effective_routing` merges an un-prefixed\n  built-in id OVER the packaged entry field-by-field (`llm/criteria/overlay.py:320-360`), so a\n  packaged posture flip survives. No overlay edit; asserted by test.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json`,\n`docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md`,\n`docs/experiments/replay_code_v4_would_block.py`, `tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_routing.py`\n(new).\n\n## Testing\nThe new test asserts, against the packaged routing: explicit entries for both ids; neither in\n`registry.OVERLAY_IDS`; both in `registry.effective_criteria()`; the repo overlay does not clobber\nthe packaged `concurrency` posture; routing-vs-document parity; and a routing-derived replay\nblocking set. `test_code_review_ws5.py`, `test_code_review_nit_routing.py`,\n`test_code_review_blocking_replay.py`, `test_criteria_snapshot.py` pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `correctness` and `edge-cases` have explicit base-reviewer routing entries, are absent from\n  `OVERLAY_IDS`, and appear in `registry.effective_criteria()`, with the repo overlay leaving\n  the packaged `concurrency` posture intact; checked by\n  `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_criteria_routing.py -q` (that file is\n  absent today, so the command errors now).\n- [ ] The calibration document records, for each of `correctness`, `edge-cases` and `concurrency` at\n  0.54: would-block findings, changes hit, % of all changes, mean validity, and whether\n  `c3aec3eae6` / `d2dea317ec` are recalled; checked by\n  `grep -n \"Code-v4 friction replay at 0.54\" docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md`\n  (no match today) plus the parity assertion in the same pytest run.\n- [ ] Every criterion flipped to `blocking_enabled: true` records a measured % of all changes at or\n  under 8.0%, and every criterion left advisory records its measured number; checked by the\n  routing-vs-document parity assertion in that pytest run.\n- [ ] `replay_code_v4_would_block.py` derives its blocking set from the packaged routing and still\n  exits 0 corpus-free; checked by\n  `grep -n \"^_BLOCKING_SET = (\" docs/experiments/replay_code_v4_would_block.py` returning nothing (it\n  matches line 45 today) and `.venv/bin/python docs/experiments/replay_code_v4_would_block.py`\n  exiting 0."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787371211759008001,"uuid":"8a692c76-d018-4f87-bbcc-0fa413169503"}